    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 741172,
      "summarized_text": "The discussion concerns how to interpret Shopify Orders CSV discount and refund fields without overstating deductions. One reply describes **Line item discount** as a product-level reduction, **Discount amount** as an order-level total, and **Refunded amount** as money returned to the customer; these values can overlap, especially when refunds affect revenue. A later clarification stresses that Discount amount and Refunded amount are order-level values repeated on every item row, while Line item discount is row-level and can be summed across lines. Summing repeated order-level values can therefore multiply them by the number of items. The suggested reporting approach is to sum line-item discounts, select each order-level value only once per order, and never add all three fields together. Check whether Subtotal is already net of discounts before subtracting discounts again. The CSV may not reliably allocate partial refunds by SKU; use Shopify’s Admin API or a specialized export app when line-level refund detail is required. The discussion offers practical guidance but recommends validating field behavior against an individual order; no definitive Shopify-specific resolution is established.",
